                <pb facs="0590" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg584"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24551U/7: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Brazzaville (Taylor)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-21T21:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Department’s 85, August 3, 9 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d571-f1"/> War
                    Department has been informed by a member of General Bolte’s staff in London that
                    General Valin, de Gaulle’s Air Chief, has said he fears disagreeable incidents
                    will occur if American aircraft or personnel arrive at Pointe Noire before
                    agreement is reached on Fighting French request for eight liaison aircraft. This
                    may merely be an effort to exert pressure on War Department. Please telegraph
                    immediately whether you consider that such a statement is to be taken
                    seriously.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
